<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Bush returns seven weeks after radioactive iodine. He stopped methimazole three days before the treatment and has not restarted it. For about two weeks he has felt more tired in the afternoons, a little cold in air-conditioned rooms, and slightly constipated, and he has regained 2.2 kg. He has had no palpitations, and his home pulse checks have been regular. He takes metoprolol and apixaban every day, with no bleeding. He has started running again, two miles three days a week, without symptoms. He has no neck pain, eye symptoms, or swallowing trouble. He knows of no snoring and has no daytime sleepiness. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Since radioactive iodine</td><td>Tiredness, mild cold intolerance, and constipation for about two weeks; weight up 2.2 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Rhythm</td><td>No palpitations; regular pulse on home checks</td></tr><tr><td>Apixaban safety</td><td>No bleeding; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Activity</td><td>Running two miles three days a week</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>No snoring or daytime sleepiness</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

