  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypothyroidism after radioactive iodine (E89.0)</content>. Free T4 0.6 ng/dL and total T3 78 ng/dL are low, with TSH rising to 5.6 mIU/L, and he has early hypothyroid symptoms: the expected result of radioactive iodine for Graves&apos; disease. [S]<list><item>Start levothyroxine 75 mcg daily on an empty stomach, below full replacement because of his age and recent atrial fibrillation.</item><item>TSH and free T4 in eight weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Graves&apos; disease treated with radioactive iodine (E05.00)</content>. No longer thyrotoxic; no eye disease. [S]<list><item>Eye symptoms to be reported promptly; eye examination at the yearly review.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Paroxysmal atrial fibrillation, in sinus rhythm (I48.0)</content>. Sinus rhythm with a resting rate of 64 now that he is no longer thyrotoxic. Sleep apnea screen negative (STOP-BANG 2). [S]<list><item>Reduce metoprolol succinate to 25 mg daily for eight weeks, then stop.</item><item>Continue apixaban for now; wear a 14-day ECG patch in about five weeks, once thyroid levels are closer to normal, and decide about apixaban at the next visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Heart rate and rhythm</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>64 per minute, regular</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Every visit; target below 130/80</td><td>Completed today</td><td>128/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>88.6 kg, BMI 25.1; up 2.2 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Atrial fibrillation symptoms</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Ambulatory rhythm monitoring</td><td>As symptoms or decisions require</td><td>Ordered</td><td>14-day ECG patch in about five weeks, to confirm sinus rhythm before the anticoagulation decision</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Anticoagulant adherence and bleeding</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses; no bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>CHA2DS2-VASc and HAS-BLED</td><td>Yearly and with any change in clinical status</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Unchanged: CHA2DS2-VASc 1, HAS-BLED 1</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Alcohol, tobacco, and physical activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No alcohol; never used tobacco; running two miles three days a week</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Sleep apnea symptom screen</td><td>At diagnosis and at least yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>STOP-BANG 2: low risk; no sleep study needed. Completed two months late; no harm resulted, as the screen is negative. Corrective action: the screen is now on the atrial fibrillation intake checklist</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Free T4 and total T3 after radioactive iodine</td><td>Within one to two months of treatment, then every four to six weeks until stable</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Free T4 0.6 ng/dL and total T3 78 ng/dL, both low; TSH 5.6 mIU/L</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Hypothyroid and overtreatment symptoms</td><td>Every visit during titration</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tiredness, cold intolerance, and constipation; no palpitations or tremor</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>TSH after starting levothyroxine</td><td>Four to eight weeks after each dose change</td><td>Due</td><td>Due in eight weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Levothyroxine timing and interactions</td><td>At the start of treatment and with new medicines</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taken alone on an empty stomach; no calcium, iron, or acid-suppressing medicine</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Resting heart rate below 110 per minute without palpitations while thyrotoxic. Outcome by 1991-05-20: Heart rate 72 in sinus rhythm on metoprolol two weeks after intake [S]</item><item>No atrial fibrillation once no longer thyrotoxic, confirmed by ambulatory monitoring before the anticoagulation decision. In progress; target 1991-09-11 [S]</item><item>TSH within 0.4 to 4.0 mIU/L on levothyroxine. In progress; target 1991-10-16 [S]</item><item>Back to running three miles several days a week without symptoms. In progress; target 1991-09-11 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2023 ACC/AHA/ACCP/HRS Guideline for the Diagnosis and Management of Atrial Fibrillation (2023); 2016 American Thyroid Association Guidelines for Diagnosis and Management of Hyperthyroidism and Other Causes of Thyrotoxicosis (2016); Guidelines for the Treatment of Hypothyroidism: Prepared by the American Thyroid Association Task Force on Thyroid Hormone Replacement (2014); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, atrial fibrillation and hypothyroidism monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Thyroid tests and review in eight weeks, after the 14-day ECG patch. Next scheduled visit 1991-09-11: four-month review: levothyroxine titration and anticoagulation decision. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
